THE PRICE, read off this single carrier:
  * R_1 and R_2 ARE records: bit, durable, non-trivial, and each individually WRITABLE
    (max |Tr(P_E R_i)| = 0.000000 above).
  * NEITHER is INDEPENDENTLY writable: the only admissible flip is the SIMULTANEOUS one.
    Writing R_1 necessarily writes R_2.  That is exactly what was given up.
  * A non-constant invariant appears: chi_12, the CORRELATION R_1 R_2.
  * And R_1 R_2 has |Tr(P_E R_1R_2)| = 4.000000 -- it FAILS clause (iv).  It is a durable
    non-trivial bit that CANNOT BE WRITTEN BY ANY ADMISSIBLE OPERATION WHATEVER (C-11).
  * So the configuration-dependent, non-cancelling quantity this carrier buys is FROZEN
    (absolutely so at k=2, by the Part 7 theorem).
    It accumulates, it is not blind -- and nothing can create it.  It is a superselection
    charge, not a source.  This is O-42 ('writability requires energetic neutrality') and
    O-40 ('C-47's extensive quantity was bought at the cost of independent writability')
    appearing as the SAME fact, one level up, about PRODUCTS of records.

